      },
      "message": "fix(ui): Tab, Shift+Tab and Enter move between the value fields of a page\n\negui's Tab walked every focusable widget in draw order, so from a value\nfield the focus went to a group header, a combo or the action bar, and\nEnter dropped the focus.\n\nThe form seam's number helpers now register each value field, with its\ngroup, in a ring over the Properties pane (layout::field_ring). From a\nregistered field, Tab and Shift+Tab move to the next or previous field\n(wrapping), and Enter commits the value to the draft and moves to the\nnext field of the same group. The moved-to field gains the focus at the\nstart of the next frame, so its text is selected and typing replaces it.\nFocus is ephemeral UI state; values still reach the document through\nApply's command.\n\nPinned by tab_and_shift_tab_walk_the_value_fields_and_wrap,\nenter_commits_the_value_and_moves_to_the_next_field_of_its_group and\nthe field_ring rule tests.\n\nFixes #2516\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
